For position one may first shift the origin so that $\expect{X}=0$. Then $(\Delta x)^2
=
\expect{X^2}
=
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}
dx\,|\psi(x)|^2x^2.$ Positive and negative contributions cancel in $\expect{X}$, but they add in $\expect{X^2}$. A broader probability distribution therefore has a larger variance.

