p.src:
We now return to dynamics. The abstract law is $i\hbar\frac{d}{dt}\ket{\psi(t)}
=
H\ket{\psi(t)}.$ For a particle of mass $m$ in a potential $V(X)$, take $H=\frac{P^2}{2m}+V(X).$ This imports the classical kinetic-plus-potential form and then tests whether its quantum evolution reproduces classical motion in the proper regime.

