p.src:
In the position representation, $P^2$ becomes a second derivative. A function of $X$ acts by multiplication: $\bigl(V(X)\psi\bigr)(x)=V(x)\psi(x).$ Consequently, $i\hbar\frac{\partial\psi(x,t)}{\partial t}
=
\left[
-\frac{\hbar^2}{2m}\frac{\partial^2}{\partial x^2}
+V(x)
\right]\psi(x,t).$

