p.src:
The center of the position distribution is $\expect{X}
=
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}
dx\,\psi^*(x,t)\,x\,\psi(x,t).$ Differentiate it: $\frac{d}{dt}\expect{X}
=
\int dx\,
\left(
\dot{\psi}^{\,*}x\psi
+
\psi^*x\dot{\psi}
\right).$ The two terms are complex conjugates. On substituting Equations  and , the potential terms cancel because $V(x)$ is real. Integrating the kinetic terms by parts leaves $\begin{aligned}
\frac{d}{dt}\expect{X}
&=
\frac{1}{m}
\int dx\,
\psi^*
\left(-i\hbar\frac{\partial}{\partial x}\right)
\psi \notag\\
&=
\frac{\expect{P}}{m}.
\end{aligned}$

